# Never sent to a Docker build. The build context is the repo root - a pnpm
# workspace needs the root lockfile - so this file lives here.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, patterns are anchored at the context root: ".env" matches
# only ./.env, not apps/web/.env. Hence the **/ prefixes.

# Secrets. COPY . . would bake these into a layer, readable by anyone who can
# pull the image - even if a later instruction deletes the file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Installed or generated inside the image; the VM's copies would be wrong there
# and add hundreds of MB to every build's upload.
**/node_modules
**/dist
apps/api/src/generated

# Not needed to build or run anything, and every change to them would
# otherwise invalidate the build cache.
.git
docs
infra/vagrant
**/.vscode
